

# ── Commit message convention ────────────────────────────────── 72 cols ──┐
#                                                                          |
# <type>(<optional scope>): <subject>                                      |
#                                                                          |
# Subject line: 72 characters or less, imperative mood, no trailing        |
# period, lowercase after the colon.                                       |
#                                                                          |
#   feat     a new capability                                              |
#   fix      a bug fix                                                     |
#   docs     documentation only                                            |
#   refactor behaviour-preserving restructuring                            |
#   test     adding or correcting tests                                    |
#   chore    tooling, deps, housekeeping                                   |
#   perf     a performance improvement                                     |
#   ci       CI/CD pipeline changes                                        |
#   build    build system or Docker changes                                |
#   style    formatting only, no code change                               |
#   revert   reverts a previous commit                                     |
#                                                                          |
# Body (optional): blank line after the subject, wrap at 72 columns.       |
# Explain WHY, not what -- the diff already shows what changed.            |
#                                                                          |
# Breaking change: use `feat!:` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.            |
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
